@prefix gmeow:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/norms>
    a gmeow:Slice ;
    rdfs:label "norms"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The norms slice of the GMEOW ontology (core tier): GMEOW Norms Module. Core by breadth of expected use — policy, authority, condition, rubric and criterion are load-bearing for approval, guidance, decision support, compliance and assessment across every prescription/enactment domain, so downstream core slices may take real rdfs:range and rdfs:subClassOf edges into these terms. Anatomy, dependencies, and consumer are declared in this manifest; the manifest is the sole source of slice identity and tier."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/norms> ;
    dcterms:title "GMEOW Norms Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    dcterms:creator "Blackcat Informatics® Inc." ;
    gmeow:sliceTier gmeow:tierCore ;
    gmeow:sliceProfile "narrative" ;
    gmeow:sliceDependsOn
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/kernel> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/teleology> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/temporal> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/events> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/observations> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/rights> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/citations> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/names> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/documents> ;
    gmeow:sliceConsumer "The lbox principia importer ( 4-tier authority hierarchy, special-directive triggers, paradigm precedence) and policy import/export (ODRL round-trip; OPA/Rego, Cedar, XACML down-projection — deferred to the compiler-arc window with the alignment set). The rubrics facility lives in this slice (Rubric ⊑ Norm; one canonical deontic owner, Principle 4): consumers are the lm-eval-harness task projection, the principia RLAIF axes/score-anchor import, and LLM-judge score ingestion as vantage-indexed Assessments. The registers & personas facility also lives here (expressesNorm → Norm, activatedIn → Condition; same single-owner rationale): consumers are system-prompt assembly (Persona × Norms × StyleGuide — the projection that replaces principia.yaml's Jinja2 role, deferred to the compiler-arc window with the alignment set) and the principia persona_modes/paradigm-activation import."@x-gmeow-english.
